-- title:
--   Gauss-type valuation rings agree on L(x)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field and $A_0 \subseteq L$ a valuation subring whose maximal ideal (as a local ring) is the principal ideal generated by an element $\varpi \in A_0$. Let $F$ be a field which is simultaneously an $L$-algebra and an $A_0$-algebra, compatibly (a scalar tower over $A_0$, $L$, $F$), and let $x \in F$. Let $V, V'$ be valuation subrings of $F$, each subject to three conditions: the image of $A_0$ under the structure map $A_0 \to F$ is contained in it; the image of $\varpi$ in $F$ lies in its set of nonunits, i.e. in its maximal ideal; and for every polynomial $P \in A_0[X]$ that is not divisible by the constant polynomial $\varpi$, both $P(x)$ and $P(x)^{-1}$ lie in it, where $P(x)$ denotes the evaluation of $P$ at $x$ through the $A_0$-algebra structure of $F$. The conclusion is that $V$ and $V'$ have the same trace on the intermediate field $L(x)$ generated over $L$ by $x$ inside $F$: for every $e$ in the subfield $L$-adjoin $\{x\}$ of $F$, one has $e \in V$ if and only if $e \in V'$.
--
--   The three conditions imposed on $V$ and $V'$ characterise the valuation subrings of $F$ of Gauss type relative to $(A_0, \varpi, x)$, for which $x$ behaves like a transcendental with value-preserving Gauss valuation; the statement says that such a valuation subring is determined on the simple extension $L(x)$ independently of any further choices. It is used in the identification of valuation subrings of function fields of modular curves arising from Gauss-type constructions, via base change to Laurent series and in the full-level case with level coprime to the residue characteristic.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_mem_iff_mem_of_mem_adjoin_simple_of_forall_aeval_inv_mem.lean

